# 2. How the Program Will Work

## Step-by-Step Flow

### Step 1 — Student Registration
Interested students register to become admission partners.

Required Details:
- Full Name
- Department
- Year
- Mobile Number
- Email ID
- UPI ID
- Aadhaar/College ID
- Bank Details (optional)

Students must agree to:
- Ethical communication policy
- No fake promises
- No misuse of university name
- No sharing of confidential data

---

### Step 2 — Training Session
Conduct a short training session covering:
- University courses
- Fee structure
- Admission process
- Communication skills
- Call scripts
- Objection handling
- WhatsApp follow-up methods
- CRM/lead tracking usage

Training Duration:
- 2 to 3 hours

Provide:
- PDF handbook
- Call script
- FAQ sheet
- Admission brochure
- Official media assets

---

### Step 3 — Lead Distribution
IIEC team distributes leads to students.

Lead Sources:
- Website inquiries
- Social media campaigns
- Walk-in inquiries
- Education fairs
- Online forms
- Previous databases
- WhatsApp campaigns

Rules:
- One lead assigned to one student only.
- Leads should be tracked properly.
- Duplicate calling must be avoided.
- Leads should expire after inactivity.

Suggested Lead Allocation:
- 20–50 leads per student weekly.

---

### Step 4 — Calling & Follow-Up
Students will:
- Call leads
- Explain courses and opportunities
- Share brochures and details
- Follow up regularly
- Guide students toward registration and admission

Communication Channels:
- Phone Calls
- WhatsApp
- Email (optional)
- Instagram DM (optional)

---

### Step 5 — Conversion Verification
A conversion is considered successful only when:

1. Student completes registration.
2. ₹1,600 registration fee is paid.
3. ₹15,000 admission fee is paid.
4. Admission team verifies the payment.
5. Lead ownership matches assigned caller.

---

### Step 6 — Incentive Release
After successful verification:
- Caller receives ₹500 incentive.
- Payment should be released within:
  - Same day
  - Or within 24–48 hours.

Payment Modes:
- UPI
- Bank Transfer

Maintain proper payment records.

